1
00:00:05,562 --> 00:00:09,130
The Life Of Muhammadﷺ, The Makkan Period,

2
00:00:09,483 --> 00:00:11,123
by Imam Anwr Al-Awlaki;

3
00:00:12,778 --> 00:00:14,338
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ۝

4
00:00:14,691 --> 00:00:16,251
بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ۝

5
00:00:16,835 --> 00:00:21,835
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْرا

6
00:00:22,933 --> 00:00:29,312
We covered the story of the Islam of Demaad(ضماد), and Amr Bin Absaa(عمرو بن عبسه).

7
00:00:29,723 --> 00:00:33,963
We move on to the story of Abu Dharr رضي الله عنه.

8
00:00:35,363 --> 00:00:37,888
I'm going to mention to you the Imam Ahmad(امام احمد) version.

9
00:00:38,432 --> 00:00:46,980
Abu Dharr رضي الله عنه stated that me, my brother and my mother left our land of Ghifaar(غفار),

10
00:00:47,579 --> 00:00:52,955
 because our people used to be disrespectful of the Ash'hur-Ul-Hurum(أشهرالحرم).

11
00:00:53,509 --> 00:00:59,615
 Al-Ash'hur Ul Hurum(الاشهرالحرم) are four months, in which the Arabs used to consider sacred

12
00:01:00,196 --> 00:01:04,493
and this would give them a break from warfare.

13
00:01:05,154 --> 00:01:10,592
So, they would not allow killing, war during those four months.

14
00:01:10,986 --> 00:01:18,300
And it was a firm tradition among them that you do not break, the sanctity of these four months.

15
00:01:19,151 --> 00:01:20,961
The people of Ghiffar(غفار) were different,

16
00:01:21,273 --> 00:01:26,415
these were professional Raiders of caravans, they didn't care about Ash'hur-Ul-Hurum(أشهرالحرم) and all this stuff.

17
00:01:27,403 --> 00:01:33,057
They were Bedouins, who were raid caravans, steal, kill, corrupt,

18
00:01:33,862 --> 00:01:35,927
and they didn't follow any rules or customers.

19
00:01:36,850 --> 00:01:38,129
These are the people of Ghiffar(غفار).

20
00:01:38,744 --> 00:01:42,231
And they had a bad reputation in Arabia, I mean people in Arabia knew Ghiffar(غفار).

21
00:01:42,905 --> 00:01:45,711
These people don't abide by the rules, violent.

22
00:01:47,080 --> 00:01:52,633
Abu Dharr رضي الله عنه before Islam, he disagreed with this style of life.

23
00:01:52,801 --> 00:01:56,813
So he, his brother and mother decided to leave Ghiffar(غفار), just go out.

24
00:01:57,464 --> 00:02:03,087
So, they went and they visited an uncle of theirs, he used to be a member of a different tribe.

25
00:02:03,705 --> 00:02:08,792
And they stayed with him and Abu Dharr(ابو ذر) says he was very generous and hospitable to us , very kind.

26
00:02:10,520 --> 00:02:12,642
But his relatives were becoming jealous.

27
00:02:13,754 --> 00:02:15,487
How come he's treating us so well.

28
00:02:16,658 --> 00:02:21,539
So what they did, they went up to the uncle of Abu Dharr(ابو ذر) and they told him;

29
00:02:21,876 --> 00:02:32,165
When you are absent, Unais, Abu Dharr(ابو ذر)'s  brother, he goes and visits your wife, and he's interested in her.

30
00:02:33,501 --> 00:02:41,288
The Uncle, quite naively, he went to Abu Dharr(ابو ذر) and Unais(اٌنَيْسْ) and mentioned to them, what he heard.

31
00:02:41,839 --> 00:02:44,805
He said: People are saying that Unais(اٌنَيْسْ) is interested in my wife.

32
00:02:46,032 --> 00:02:50,427
Abu Dharr(ابو ذر) was very angry and upset, this was false.

33
00:02:51,607 --> 00:02:56,219
He was very angry and he said: All of the good what you have done to us, you have cancelled it.

34
00:02:57,013 --> 00:03:04,015
All of the hospitality, your kindness is gone, after this accusation of yours,

35
00:03:04,720 --> 00:03:07,184
and immediately packed up and left.

36
00:03:08,033 --> 00:03:14,363
Abu Dharr(ابو ذر) said: My uncle was quite sorry and regretful for what he done and he wrapped himself in a cloth and he was crying.

37
00:03:14,923 --> 00:03:17,463
But Abu Dharr(ابو ذر) said: We were so angry and we just left.

38
00:03:18,867 --> 00:03:21,032
And now they settled the place close to Makkah.

39
00:03:22,010 --> 00:03:25,330
Abu Dharr(ابو ذر) says that my brother, Unais(اٌنَيْسْ), he went to do some business in Makkah.

40
00:03:26,165 --> 00:03:30,883
And he met a man who claims to be a Prophet, he met Muhammadﷺ.

41
00:03:32,273 --> 00:03:38,656
So, Unais(اٌنَيْسْ) came back and he said, I found the man who was preaching a new religion, worshipping Allah alone.

42
00:03:39,401 --> 00:03:46,798
Abu Dharr(ابو ذر) said: And at that time, I have already worshipped Allah for three years,

43
00:03:47,428 --> 00:03:52,043
and revoked all of the worshipping of idols, I renounced it.

44
00:03:52,260 --> 00:03:58,538
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), you see these people, their Fitrah(فطرة), guides them and tells them that this is wrong, this is false.

45
00:03:59,268 --> 00:04:02,974
Abu Dharr(ابو ذر) says: I've been praying to Allah for three years.

46
00:04:04,523 --> 00:04:08,158
So, Abu Dharr(ابو ذر) was asked, how would you praying to Allah, he said:

47
00:04:08,317 --> 00:04:12,771
 I would pray to whichever direction Allah would points me to,

48
00:04:13,238 --> 00:04:16,654
and I would pray in whatever way Allah guide me to,

49
00:04:17,021 --> 00:04:19,962
and I would pray at night until I fall asleep,

50
00:04:20,456 --> 00:04:22,582
and only the sun would wake me up in the morning.

51
00:04:22,988 --> 00:04:27,151
So, he would pray, he doesn't know how to pray, but he would pray to Allah سبحانه وتعالى, for three years.

52
00:04:28,112 --> 00:04:30,373
Abu Dharr(ابو ذر) asked, his brother Unais(اٌنَيْسْ), he said:

53
00:04:31,245 --> 00:04:32,345
what does he teach?

54
00:04:32,526 --> 00:04:36,393
So, Unais(اٌنَيْسْ) mentioned some of the teachings of Islam that he learned from Rasool Allah ﷺ.

55
00:04:36,567 --> 00:04:39,329
And then he asked him, What are the people saying about him?

56
00:04:39,701 --> 00:04:43,915
Unais(اٌنَيْسْ) said: They're claiming that he's a sorcerer, and magician, a liar, and he went down the list.

57
00:04:44,677 --> 00:04:45,501
Abu Dharr(ابو ذر) said:

58
00:04:45,580 --> 00:04:46,854
مَا اَشْفَيْتَ غَلِيْلِيْ

59
00:04:47,175 --> 00:04:49,158
You haven't satisfied my hunger.

60
00:04:50,556 --> 00:04:53,382
I want to go and investigate the matter myself.

61
00:04:54,708 --> 00:04:57,728
What the people say might not necessarily be right.

62
00:04:58,310 --> 00:05:06,070
The media of Makkah, the CNN of the day, or the ABC or whatever you call it, had all of these labels that they would brand Rasool Allahﷺ with

63
00:05:06,523 --> 00:05:13,965
but Abu Dharr(ابو ذر) did not have trust in what the people are saying, he would have to go and meet Rasool Allahﷺ

64
00:05:14,425 --> 00:05:16,428
and hear it from the messenger himself.

65
00:05:17,534 --> 00:05:21,309
And that is what the Muslim is required to do.

66
00:05:21,848 --> 00:05:22,569
تَبَيَّنُوْا

67
00:05:23,047 --> 00:05:27,483
 Allah سبحانه وتعالى says; when you receive some information verify it, Tabayyanoo(تَبَيَّنُوْا).

68
00:05:28,356 --> 00:05:32,759
And that's where our scholars learn the science of Hadith(حديث).

69
00:05:33,645 --> 00:05:34,811
They would verify.

70
00:05:35,033 --> 00:05:38,509
It's not just enough to hear a Hadith(حديث) narrated from someone.

71
00:05:38,944 --> 00:05:40,192
The scholars used to say:

72
00:05:40,232 --> 00:05:43,301
 هَاتُوا رِجَالَكُمْ اَوْ سَمُّوْلَنَا رِجَالَكُمْ

73
00:05:43,628 --> 00:05:47,146
Whenever they would hear a Hadith(حديث), they would say mention, the names of your men.

74
00:05:47,741 --> 00:05:48,862
Where did you hear this from?

75
00:05:49,034 --> 00:05:52,804
Tell us the names, we want to know who you got this information from?

76
00:05:53,381 --> 00:05:55,647
We just don't follow any hearsay.

77
00:05:57,682 --> 00:06:01,516
Abu Dharr(ابو ذر), he said: I went into Makkah and I asked the first man I saw in front of me.

78
00:06:01,556 --> 00:06:04,384
I told them Can you please guide me towards Muhammadﷺ.

79
00:06:04,672 --> 00:06:09,203
He said that man immediately started calling the men is Quraish(قُرَيْشْ)

80
00:06:09,267 --> 00:06:15,135
 and they started pelting me with stones, rocks, whatever they could get their hands on, until I fell unconscious.

81
00:06:16,555 --> 00:06:19,596
He said: By the time I woke up, I was like

82
00:06:19,636 --> 00:06:20,960
 نُصبْ اَحْمَرْ

83
00:06:21,748 --> 00:06:24,812
Nusub(نصب) the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), they used to have these stones

84
00:06:25,225 --> 00:06:29,057
idols which, they would slaughter and sacrifice their animals over.

85
00:06:29,336 --> 00:06:31,019
So, they would be soaked with blood.

86
00:06:32,214 --> 00:06:37,995
That's the description Abu Dharr(ابو ذر) gave of himself like a red pole, soaked with blood from head to toe.

87
00:06:38,722 --> 00:06:42,918
He said: So I went to the well of Zam-Zam(زمزم), I drank water and I washed the blood of my body.

88
00:06:43,593 --> 00:06:45,111
And then I went next to the Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).

89
00:06:45,785 --> 00:06:49,212
In the narration of Imam Ahmad(اِمَامْ اَحْمَدْ), it says that he stayed there for 30 days,

90
00:06:50,336 --> 00:06:52,835
 not knowing where to meet Rasool Allah ﷺ.

91
00:06:53,927 --> 00:07:01,627
And Abu Dharr(ابو ذر) said: I did not have any food for the entire period, except for drinking the water of Zam-Zam(زمزم).

92
00:07:03,754 --> 00:07:10,976
Now, I think physicians can tell us that a person can survive by drinking water for quite a while.

93
00:07:11,619 --> 00:07:14,274
So, maybe that's not such a surprise.

94
00:07:14,690 --> 00:07:17,579
But the surprising thing is what comes next,

95
00:07:18,330 --> 00:07:19,554
Abu Dharr(ابو ذر) said:

96
00:07:20,021 --> 00:07:22,055
And I started picking up weight,

97
00:07:22,554 --> 00:07:25,045
until I was getting folds on my stomach.

98
00:07:26,391 --> 00:07:31,494
You know for them the Bedouins, they would have flat tummies, they were very fit.

99
00:07:32,303 --> 00:07:36,461
Abu Dharr(ابو ذر) said: I was gaining weight and now the flesh on my stomach was folding.

100
00:07:36,564 --> 00:07:39,027
You know when you sit down and the flesh on the stomach folds.!

101
00:07:40,162 --> 00:07:43,337
Abu Dharr(ابو ذر) states that he then saw two women,

102
00:07:44,097 --> 00:07:48,177
making Tawaf(طواف) and they would touch Isaaf(إساف) and Naila(نائله) on every turn.

103
00:07:48,946 --> 00:07:50,454
What's the story of Isaaf(إساف) and Naila(نائله)?

104
00:07:50,494 --> 00:07:58,946
Isaaf(إساف) and Naila(نائله) are a man and a woman, who were in love and they couldn't get married.

105
00:08:00,002 --> 00:08:04,091
And they had an appointment, a date to meet next to Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه),

106
00:08:05,090 --> 00:08:08,646
and they intended to fornicate next to the house of Allah.

107
00:08:09,324 --> 00:08:12,887
Allah سبحانه وتعالى turned them into stones, on the spot.

108
00:08:14,141 --> 00:08:19,118
After the passage of sometime the Mushrikeen(مشركين) of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), started worshipping them,

109
00:08:20,095 --> 00:08:22,514
started worshipping these two stones, Isaaf(إساف) and Naila(نائله).

110
00:08:22,994 --> 00:08:30,019
To show you how, when you open the floodgates for Shaytaan(شيطان), you can't close it, he just throws you in dungeons of darkness,

111
00:08:30,997 --> 00:08:37,480
can never get out of it, it's spiral, if you get in, you'll never come out, darkness over darkness, one veil after another.

112
00:08:37,930 --> 00:08:45,138
Now, the story of idol worshipping actually started as erecting statues after righteous men die.

113
00:08:45,579 --> 00:08:50,725
Shaytaan(شيطان) came to the people of Noah(نوح) and told them after the righteous men have passed away.

114
00:08:52,128 --> 00:08:54,921
Why don't you erect statues of these righteous men?

115
00:08:54,941 --> 00:08:57,641
So, that they would remind you about Allah.

116
00:08:58,646 --> 00:09:00,288
He came to teach them good.

117
00:09:00,399 --> 00:09:03,336
He said: They would remind you about Allah سبحانه وتعالى, so they did that.

118
00:09:03,891 --> 00:09:07,285
And then after a few generations, he started telling them, worship them.

119
00:09:08,756 --> 00:09:11,208
That's how the idol worshipping grew.

120
00:09:13,240 --> 00:09:15,729
So, here you have Isaaf(إساف) and Naila(نائله) been worshiped,

121
00:09:15,842 --> 00:09:19,955
and these two women would make Tawaf(طواف) and they would touch Isaaf(إساف) and Naila(نائله) on every turn.

122
00:09:20,328 --> 00:09:24,063
Now Abu Dharr(ابو ذر), he despised idol worshipping.

123
00:09:24,400 --> 00:09:25,932
So, he threw out a comment.

124
00:09:26,539 --> 00:09:30,581
He said: Why don't you make one of them have intercourse with the other?

125
00:09:31,565 --> 00:09:37,474
Either the woman did not understand, what he said or they didn't believe what they heard.

126
00:09:38,151 --> 00:09:39,157
They continued.

127
00:09:40,041 --> 00:09:42,823
When Abu Dharr(ابو ذر) saw that his words, did not deter them.

128
00:09:43,366 --> 00:09:47,002
He threw out and even cruder comment,

129
00:09:47,337 --> 00:09:48,773
and I'm not gonna mention it.

130
00:09:49,431 --> 00:09:55,105
Now the woman were sure of what they heard, they immediately just started running and screaming,

131
00:09:55,997 --> 00:10:00,347
wailing down the streets of Makkah and who did they run into?

132
00:10:00,499 --> 00:10:02,364
Muhammadﷺ and Abu Bakr(ابوبكر)

133
00:10:03,569 --> 00:10:07,258
Muhammadﷺ and Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) are seeing these two women running in the streets, screaming.

134
00:10:08,234 --> 00:10:09,343
What's wrong with you?

135
00:10:10,337 --> 00:10:13,557
They said that heretic over there,

136
00:10:14,484 --> 00:10:16,806
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: What's the matter with him?

137
00:10:17,079 --> 00:10:19,908
They said: He spoke a word that fills the mouth.

138
00:10:20,429 --> 00:10:21,397
تَمْلَأ الفَهمْ

139
00:10:21,437 --> 00:10:25,191
In other words something that is unspeakable, very bad words.

140
00:10:26,615 --> 00:10:34,321
Rasool Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), they went to meet this man, Abu Dharr رضي الله عنه and they started the conversation.

141
00:10:35,571 --> 00:10:39,043
Rasool Allah ﷺ asked Abu Dharr(ابو ذر): Where are you from?

142
00:10:39,603 --> 00:10:42,358
مِنْ اَيْنَ الرَّجُلْ، قَالَ اَنَا مِنْ غَفَّارْ

143
00:10:42,643 --> 00:10:44,931
He said: I am from Ghifaar(غفار).

144
00:10:46,267 --> 00:10:49,035
Rasool Allah ﷺ placed his hands on his forehead.

145
00:10:49,926 --> 00:10:52,970
Abu Dharr(ابو ذر) said: Rasool Allah ﷺ was surprised and amazed

146
00:10:53,846 --> 00:10:59,464
to see somebody from Ghifaar(غفار) coming to Makkah, in search of the truth, from Ghifaar(غفار)!

147
00:11:00,107 --> 00:11:09,787
These people who raid caravans, the ones who do not follow any rules or any customs, and he is searching for the truth in Makkah

148
00:11:09,876 --> 00:11:16,937
 and the people of Makkah, the ones who are considered to be the religious authority of Arabia, are rejecting my message.

149
00:11:17,708 --> 00:11:19,766
فَكَرِهَا اَنْ اِنْتَسَبْتُ اِلَى غِفَارْ

150
00:11:20,221 --> 00:11:24,771
Abu Dharr(ابو ذر) said: I felt that he might have disliked that I mentioned that I'm from Ghifaar(غفار).

151
00:11:25,020 --> 00:11:29,205
So, I extended my hand to pull his hand from his forehead.

152
00:11:29,914 --> 00:11:33,545
Abu Dharr(ابو ذر) said: Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) slammed my hand and told me, put your hand down.

153
00:11:35,787 --> 00:11:39,676
And then the conversation continued and Abu Dharr(ابو ذر) ended up embracing Islam.

154
00:11:41,076 --> 00:11:43,075
Rasool Allah ﷺ told Abu Dharr(ابو ذر):

155
00:11:43,234 --> 00:11:44,044
اُكْتُمْ اِيْمَانَكْ

156
00:11:44,139 --> 00:11:45,861
Keep your Eeman(ايمان) secret.

157
00:11:46,807 --> 00:11:51,086
Abu Dharr(ابو ذر), he went out the next day rather than keeping his Eeman(ايمان) secret,

158
00:11:51,111 --> 00:11:53,583
he went in front of the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) and said:

159
00:11:53,659 --> 00:11:56,549
اَشْهَدُ الله اله الَّا الله وَ اَشْهَدُ اَنَّ محمد الرَّسُول الله

160
00:11:56,939 --> 00:11:58,456
He doesn't care about the consequences.

161
00:12:00,333 --> 00:12:06,394
He said: They gathered around me and they beat me up, so bad, I was gonna die.

162
00:12:07,250 --> 00:12:11,464
Until, Al-Abbas Bin Abdul-Muttalib(العباس بن عبدالمطلب) came in and said, Do you know where this man is from?

163
00:12:11,892 --> 00:12:12,982
Just one question,

164
00:12:13,392 --> 00:12:14,281
he is from Ghifaar(غفار).

165
00:12:14,440 --> 00:12:17,066
Abu Dharr(ابو ذر) said: Immediately they just ran away.

166
00:12:18,051 --> 00:12:21,287
All what you would see is them fleeing, running away from him.

167
00:12:22,461 --> 00:12:24,395
But he did the same thing next day,

168
00:12:25,072 --> 00:12:26,662
and he did the same thing third day,

169
00:12:27,046 --> 00:12:29,760
and every day the same thing would happen they would come and beat him up,

170
00:12:29,830 --> 00:12:35,370
until Al-Abbas(العباس) comes and tells this new group of people who are hitting him that the man is from Ghifaar(غفار).

171
00:12:36,165 --> 00:12:43,689
Al-Abbas(العباس) said: And you know if this man gets killed by you, that none of your trade will make it safely to Syria.

172
00:12:45,359 --> 00:12:46,657
They gonna take revenge of you.

173
00:12:47,364 --> 00:12:53,798
Rasool Allah ﷺ then told Abu Dharr(ابو ذر), Go back to your people and convey the message to them.

174
00:12:54,381 --> 00:12:56,508
And when you hear that I prevailed, come to me.

175
00:12:57,881 --> 00:13:00,664
How long did Abu Dharr(ابو ذر) stay with Rasool Allah ﷺ.?

176
00:13:00,738 --> 00:13:01,492
Quite a short time.

177
00:13:01,532 --> 00:13:03,113
How much did he learn from him?

178
00:13:04,202 --> 00:13:05,531
Probably not a lot.

179
00:13:06,327 --> 00:13:08,983
Few verses, a few Ahadith(احاديث) here and there and that was it.

180
00:13:10,258 --> 00:13:12,622
Abu Dharr(ابو ذر), he went back to his people, Ghifaar(غفار).

181
00:13:13,506 --> 00:13:16,283
And he started giving them Da'wah(دعوة),

182
00:13:16,918 --> 00:13:23,066
slowly and slowly, people were accepting Islam, among the people of Ghifaar(غفار).

183
00:13:24,856 --> 00:13:29,778
He said, by the time Rasool Allah ﷺ made Hijrah(هجرة) almost half of my tribe were Muslim,

184
